#: ../../running/settings.rst:2 ef907cbba06b41cfa96fafe403451d2c
msgid "How big a new cartridge is"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:4 69f87a12b6ad4a81a38116351906de4d
msgid ""
"A new cartridge is **1,000 MB**, whatever generation it is. A real LTO-8 "
"holds 12 TB, and the console will make you one that does — but not by "
"default, and this page is why, and how to change it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:13 e650d2d8658b4c8985766e95d21743e4
msgid "Why not the real capacity"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:15 36016c0f8c4941b0892614f72f846e7d
msgid ""
"It costs nothing in disk. MHVTL's media files are sparse: a cartridge "
"occupies only what has been written to it, so a 12 TB tape and a 1 GB "
"tape both start at a few kilobytes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:19 162039eb6b52435e86624a1a285678e6
msgid "It costs time, and that is the problem."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:21 f090a9643e8a4223aff03a3eca594c10
msgid "How long it takes to fill one, at about 55 MB/s"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:25 c6ea3b1ca2ff43c9b00d021588fd60e8
msgid "Cartridge"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:26 bc8687c47d8b4b02a9ed7d3619a61d5a
msgid "Time to fill"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:27 c5b93651be7e42feba08e49b22e35fb1
msgid "1,000 MB — the default"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:28 dcd692e2dc8144d4b44462320fad2c56
msgid "18 seconds"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:29 671d1255eea04fedbe17c80d1eb7e76c
msgid "LTO-6 at its real 2.5 TB"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:30 01d2d2f16598484c8dc03be745757d0d
msgid "13 hours"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:31 89fee03866874dafaf56a0503f741894
msgid "LTO-8 at its real 12 TB"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:32 4eca5888dc5e40e3bc4c2f0a3178f602
msgid "**63 hours**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:34 c28ba88611814e8fbaf64eb083a50ed5
msgid ""
"The things a virtual tape library is usually *for* are what happens at "
"the end of a tape: does the backup span to the next cartridge, does it "
"ask for one, does the drive report end of medium. On a cartridge nobody "
"can fill, none of that can be reached. The fullness bar never moves "
"either."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:39 8bbb0571bc7348889e2ebbd7a288c04b
msgid ""
"So the console makes a small cartridge and lets you say when you want a "
"real one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:44 4eec80482983482b9ca64bdc01119df1
msgid ""
"This decides how big the console *makes* a cartridge. It does not change "
"what the hardware holds. An LTO-8 holds 12 TB whatever is set here, and "
"that figure is shown beside every setting — the **THE CARTRIDGE HOLDS** "
"column below, and a column on the Settings page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:50 722f427a1a45471fad86709792ba4f77
msgid "Changing it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:53 3112e27518284d15898d0e475926aacd
msgid "In the console"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:55 75269543706445e1acc9f9852f32051e
msgid ""
"**System Console → Settings**. A row per cartridge type, with what it "
"will be made at, where that value came from, and what the cartridge "
"really holds — click that capacity to put it in the field."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:59 2eb2833f91ac47b0b09c1ee9330ace87
msgid ""
"A row left empty takes the default. The field accepts ``2000GB`` and "
"``12TB`` as well as a number of megabytes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:63 f5f94f36f6634f819889b993d5d512c9
msgid "From the terminal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:65 bc9d3cb202854e7f940d5e4e06a49f24
msgid ""
"There are thirty-three cartridge types, so ``list`` takes a section, a "
"family or one key — and the case never matters:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:83 4121a02d8cdd4b938b1a0a7bb5c9fd8f
msgid "``mhvtl settings list``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:83 b796e993021848069cf59f2007acd332
msgid "all thirty-three"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:84 fba9c2b10b74455bb95b4019eb2bf627
msgid "``mhvtl settings list tape.size``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:84 31c71901791f4f3abebbea1f5f273de9
msgid "the section"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:85 843a35c67fe44d6d883be2e4cc6547b6
msgid "``mhvtl settings list tape.size.lto``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:85 a8d7db92f9d74914ade18933b5dd7b0c
msgid "every LTO generation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:86 92cedbedce9a4acebfd93c58352e231b
msgid "``mhvtl settings list tape.size.3592``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:86 aeaa1304505d494288db4b410cab457a
msgid "J1A, E05, E06, E07"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:87 c405d7eb4ac1465a8ee859f0cfb646ab
msgid "``mhvtl settings list tape.size.LTO8``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:87 80abe2bd13874049b4f1e0ce6296a423
msgid "one"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:90 e559dcc38b844eebbf69fd38b98a6e40
msgid ""
"A family is not always the start of the name: the 3592 cartridges are "
"called after the drive generation that writes them, so ``tape.size.3592``"
" finds four cartridges that share no spelling with each other."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:94 c966be4da7b84c91a741ee9c489a3128
msgid "One of them on its own:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:103 124ef50001a84101bf6eff481dd3d270
msgid "Changing one, and putting it back:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:114 dda010e21874483f948c7275f07f6b35
msgid "``tape.size.default`` changes every generation at once:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:120 f232baa43a494ddbb8ef341e18374ef5
msgid ""
"``reset`` means *back to the shipped default*, not back to the real "
"capacity. The real capacity is a value you choose, like any other."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:123 f9df228bfbf14cc692454a6d129b00b2
msgid ""
"The **FROM** column names which of them answered — ``the shipped "
"default``, ``the file default``, or ``set for this density``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:127 d1782af487dc4b768edc74e7022ed00c
msgid "Just this one cartridge"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:129 3fe36432db984373a7986c68dc12af85
msgid ""
"Nothing above is needed to make a single full-size tape. Every creation "
"takes a size, and it beats whatever the settings say:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:138 3f225bac0d514010ba2a841ecfbc5c11
msgid ""
"A library can hold two kinds of cartridge, and then one size for all of "
"them is the wrong answer. ``--media-size`` gives each kind its own, and a"
" kind not named takes its setting:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:148 bfcc7e6333494ccfa9ef088e9bb8645b
msgid ""
"The creation wizard has the same field on each cartridge row, and the "
"tape form has one for the single tape."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:152 4e17034154e04cc19f23478fd22cddc2
msgid "Which setting wins"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:154 a754e980a7484c80a89c7d677602a33f
msgid ""
"Four answers, each narrower than the last. The last one that applies is "
"the one used:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:162 239f792824e343cfb0812c2251369508
msgid "Where"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:163 0c77922784374f93a627e01c32684c34
msgid "What it covers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:164 138bdb450d43453d921e24dda5328966
msgid "1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:165 f4337d40e06b4b1f8dfa7e4f6786d0d6
msgid "the console itself"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:166 e9d4c3e2c5eb424b8f230557f77c5036
msgid "1,000 MB, every generation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:167 e3dd65efb3fe4d62b0479472c5025744
msgid "2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:168 0701e7eb502d40178483d802e7280aee
msgid "``tape.size.default``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:169 9adf3f306527461880a177acce7ccd7d
msgid "every generation, on this host"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:170 75b2ca5c50c042af955f1149139fb248
msgid "3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:171 75934f2e290345cc812343357300f970
msgid "``tape.size.LTO8``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:172 1e1c1ad272a240de90937b9f160e9bba
msgid "one generation, on this host"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:173 aa58d280c59e41afae76045957a268c5
msgid "4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:174 aabc8e7655524bd1b94b78c2617b723c
msgid "``--size-mb``, or the form"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:175 81a3f9d01c964340b8af4d372042fd78
msgid "one cartridge, once"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:177 e2166195a9f54be48f8f334f5cb01b6a
msgid ""
"``mhvtl settings list`` prints which of them answered, in the **FROM** "
"column, because \"why is this cartridge 1 GB\" is the question worth "
"being able to answer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:182 2dc9426c0f414acc8b9ba32d082b7c87
msgid "Units"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:184 a9817e5befec4aab82b9d355e5fdd031
msgid ""
"Everywhere a size is given — the setting, the two flags, and both forms —"
" takes the same three spellings, and ``MB`` is assumed when there is no "
"unit:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:191 2f7f6ca6a6bc48ea9439269747187f66
msgid ""
"They are **decimal**: 1 GB is 1,000 MB. That is how tape capacity is "
"quoted — an LTO-8 is sold as 12 TB and that is 12,000,000 MB."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:194 c5f52c5021124131b7fecde5b47bfd55
msgid "``MiB``, ``GiB`` and ``TiB`` are refused rather than converted:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:201 fb3868a3745148e9954952a38895f4cc
msgid ""
"12 TB and 12 TiB are ten per cent apart, and a cartridge ten per cent off"
" the one you meant is a difference you would only find later."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:204 cf567057518341f995fb18d506955544
msgid "Sizes are stored in MB, whatever you type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:207 56c11abca56d4938a18e9b602fddabb6
msgid "The file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:209 bb0f0fcce52141938073d5ab0c0cedd6
msgid ""
"``/etc/mhvtl-gui/settings.toml``. There is no such file until you save "
"something; without one, every cartridge is 1,000 MB."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:219 aafe29eedc2a4520b2427942c50ea772
msgid ""
"It is safe to edit by hand, and each generation's real capacity is "
"written beside it as a comment, so a value can be put back without "
"looking it up. The comments are rewritten every time the console saves, "
"so they cannot go stale."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:223 115372b96ed047d0882936f7ee2d2fe5
msgid ""
"``/etc/mhvtl-gui/settings.toml.example`` beside it lists every generation"
" with its real capacity. **An upgrade replaces the example**, so do not "
"keep settings there — copy a line into ``settings.toml`` instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:227 5bf141c14bbb488e8c5eda27b2bef127
msgid "Deleting ``settings.toml`` puts every cartridge back to 1,000 MB."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:230 01be5f19e6094c27a8d831e543ab1f5f
msgid "What it does not touch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:232 48348dcbea424a1c97552a3513372e35
msgid ""
"**Cartridges you already have.** They keep the size they were made with; "
"``mhvtl tape list <library>`` shows it. A setting applies to tapes "
"created afterwards."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:236 dc762c5fca1d42c797d77346b8639e54
msgid ""
"**What the hardware holds.** The capacities come from MHVTL's own tables "
"and are not editable anywhere in the console. The *the cartridge holds* "
"column reads those."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/settings.rst:242 098e81bedabb43e0a83790fb1f6840a7
msgid ""
":doc:`../tapes/create` for making cartridges, and "
":doc:`../libraries/create` for a library's own."
msgstr ""

